{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:45:30.561Z","data":{"text":"Every acceptance line is done and both verifies pass.\n\nSummary of work:\n\n- **`src/cli/mcp-tools.ts`** — `createMcpTools(target, slices = SLICES)` now returns the nine planning tools (from a new unexported `planningTools(target)` helper) followed by each slice's `tools(target)` in registry order, throwing `slice <slice>: tool <name> is already defined` on a repeated name. The nine-tool list was moved into the helper and made data-driven so `createMcpTools` stays well under 80 lines and the file at 241 lines (under 250). Doc tags add `@scenario cli-foundation: Slice tools follow the planning tools`, `@adr 015`, and `@adr 016`, keeping `@adr 014`.\n- **`tests/mcp-tools.test.ts`** — only the \"lists exactly the nine planning tools in order\" test now passes `[]`.\n- **`tests/mcp-slice-tools.test.ts`** (new) — proves all four rows of \"Slice tools follow the planning tools\" on a local temp target, asserting tool-name order and that each slice's `tools` receives the same target.\n\n`pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, full test suite, lint) passed, as did the task verify.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/169-slice-registries/.run/results/3.md`."}}
